WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.007 --> 00:00:02.240
- [Narrator] All right
then Stranger Things fans,

00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.480
if you're watching this
then we're assuming

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:07.930
you've had time to catch
all of Stranger Things 3.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:09.770
Well if you haven't, don't
know what you're doing

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.960
watching a video about
season three theories

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:15.712
because, fair warning, there
are a lot of spoilers to come.

00:00:15.712 --> 00:00:17.678
(banging)

00:00:17.678 --> 00:00:18.917
(intense music)

00:00:18.917 --> 00:00:20.458
- [Dustin] Copy.

00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:22.360
I repeat, copy.

00:00:22.360 --> 00:00:23.790
This is a code red.

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:26.530
- [Narrator] Okay, now we've established

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:28.840
you've seen all of Stranger Things 3.

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:30.440
Today we're gonna talk about one of

00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:32.503
the biggest shocks of the season.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:36.593
So, let's dig into the
theories around Hopper's death.

00:00:36.593 --> 00:00:40.150
Disclaimer alert, we're not
confirming or denying anything.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.350
These are purely fan theories.

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:44.370
Let's take you to episode eight.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:45.203
Quick recap.

00:00:45.203 --> 00:00:46.540
Hopper and Joyce dress as Russians

00:00:46.540 --> 00:00:48.230
to shut down the gate to the Upside Down.

00:00:48.230 --> 00:00:49.530
The thing that's letting the Mind Flayer

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:50.740
turn people into mush.

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:52.020
Hopper wins a fight, yay!

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:53.660
Tells Joyce to shut down the gate.

00:00:53.660 --> 00:00:55.840
Even though he won't be
able to get out in time.

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.200
Joyce is like, oh no.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.530
Hopper's eyes saying, do it.

00:00:58.530 --> 00:01:00.620
So she does, and it's
bye-bye to these Russians,

00:01:00.620 --> 00:01:02.570
and bye-bye to Hopper.

00:01:02.570 --> 00:01:03.700
Or is it?

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:06.090
Because this is where the theories start.

00:01:06.090 --> 00:01:08.800
Fans are a little bit
skeptical about whether

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.150
our pal Hopper is actually dead or not.

00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:12.970
Let's take a look at the
evidence fans on Reddit

00:01:12.970 --> 00:01:16.170
have compiled to support their
Hopper ain't dead theory.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.010
Reddit user HouseHeisenb3rg--

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:20.746
How do you pronounce the three as an E?

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:21.690
Uh, I don't know.

00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.393
Points out the lack of a body.

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:26.160
The way Hopper's final scene was shot,

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.810
the machine explodes with
Hopper right next to it,

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.140
but when Joyce approaches
the scene afterwards,

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:31.973
there's no body.

00:01:31.973 --> 00:01:34.025
(crying)

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:39.530
Why is this important?

00:01:39.530 --> 00:01:42.520
Well, if you go back all
the way to the first episode

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:45.240
of season three, we see
exactly what happens

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:46.984
to someone if the machine explodes.

00:01:46.984 --> 00:01:49.317
(exploding)

00:01:50.527 --> 00:01:52.130
Yuck, yeah.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.040
It's not a pretty sight.

00:01:54.040 --> 00:01:58.180
Exhibit two, according to
Reddit user Montgomery7248,

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:00.210
really loving that topic title by the way,

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.110
is the music that plays when
Eleven reads Hopper's letter.

00:02:05.251 --> 00:02:09.539
♪ I ♪

00:02:09.539 --> 00:02:12.080
♪ I will be king ♪

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:12.913
Recognize that song?

00:02:12.913 --> 00:02:15.560
Fans have pointed out
that's the same cover

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:18.280
of David Bowie's Heroes
played in season one

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.040
episode three, when Will's body was found.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:22.926
And everyone believed he was dead too.

00:02:22.926 --> 00:02:26.909
♪ I ♪

00:02:26.909 --> 00:02:30.260
♪ I will be king ♪

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.093
- It's not Will.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:32.863
It can't be.

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:35.900
- [Narrator] Of course, it
turns out Mike was right.

00:02:35.900 --> 00:02:36.743
It wasn't Will.

00:02:37.940 --> 00:02:42.170
Or, as Montgomery7248 puts it,
I can't think of any reason

00:02:42.170 --> 00:02:43.860
that they would've picked that song,

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:46.542
given the countless songs
perfect for that situation,

00:02:46.542 --> 00:02:48.980
other than them subtly calling back

00:02:48.980 --> 00:02:51.560
to another time where
we were told a character

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.233
was dead when they weren't.

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.700
If Hopper isn't dead,
where the hell is he?

00:02:57.700 --> 00:03:01.510
Fill your boots, fans have
plenty of suggestions.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:03.210
The biggie is that Hopper somehow

00:03:03.210 --> 00:03:04.840
found a way to the Upside Down.

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.869
Or as Strangerthingsideas puts it, hopped.

00:03:07.869 --> 00:03:09.610
I see what you did there.

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:12.100
That is a truly terrifying prospect

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:13.283
given what lives there.

00:03:14.724 --> 00:03:16.340
(roaring)

00:03:16.340 --> 00:03:18.190
Another popular theory is related

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.707
to the after credits scene.

00:03:19.707 --> 00:03:21.760
(speaking foreign language)

00:03:21.760 --> 00:03:22.870
Hang on, hang on.

00:03:22.870 --> 00:03:24.240
Which American?

00:03:24.240 --> 00:03:26.190
Well if you ask theupsid3down,

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:28.490
again with the threes and the Es,

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:30.940
Hopper could've landed in Russia

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:32.140
rather than the Upside down.

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:36.940
Which could mean the American
prisoner is in fact Hopper.

00:03:36.940 --> 00:03:39.990
Side note, not everyone
thinks the American is Hopper.

00:03:39.990 --> 00:03:41.400
Back to HouseHeisenb3rg,

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:44.880
who thinks the American
could be, this guy.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:47.040
Ah yes, Dr. Brenner.

00:03:47.040 --> 00:03:50.650
His fate has kinda been a
mystery since season two.

00:03:50.650 --> 00:03:52.800
We thought he was dead
at the end of season one.

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.220
But then Eleven found out
he was actually alive.

00:03:55.220 --> 00:03:57.650
According to this theory,
Brenner is the reason

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.580
the Russians knew about the Upside Down,

00:03:59.580 --> 00:04:01.500
and the gate in Hawkins.

00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:04.070
You might think, hey,
this is all well and good.

00:04:04.070 --> 00:04:06.840
But surely, in the three
months since Hopper died

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.780
in potentially mysterious circumstances,

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:12.740
Eleven would've used her
powers to look for him.

00:04:12.740 --> 00:04:14.940
Except, as some of you have pointed out,

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:17.070
her powers have gone, remember?

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:18.203
So how would she know?

00:04:19.490 --> 00:04:21.850
Whatever happened to
Hopper, it can't be good.

00:04:21.850 --> 00:04:23.900
If he's dead, well he's dead.

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:26.990
If not, he's potentially
either with the Russians,

00:04:26.990 --> 00:04:28.520
who have a hungry Demogorgon.

00:04:28.520 --> 00:04:30.810
Or in the Upside Down, with a Mind Flayer

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:32.660
who is super pissed.

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:36.819
He lost his weird bush monster body thing.

00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:38.450
(screeching)

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:40.540
Now it's over to you, what do you think?

00:04:40.540 --> 00:04:42.660
Do any of these theories hold weight?

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:44.490
Do you have any theories of your own.

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:46.130
Let us know in the comments below.

00:04:46.130 --> 00:04:48.230
You know, so we can obsess about them too.

